Hello , Brian.

I tried to contact tcltk2's maintainer through another email address with no success, but I found a solution through Gemini. After some suggested tests, I got this message from the agent:

Could not find service "org.xquartz.startx" confirms that macOS Golden Gate wiped or blocked XQuartz's LaunchAgent during the OS upgrade (a very common issue after major macOS updates, which move or clear files in /Library/LaunchAgents).

This is what solved the problem - enabling the X11 server in the background as you previously suggested (I did not know how to do it):
After installing, macOS may block org.xquartz from registering until you allow it:

  1.  Open System Settings ? General ? Login Items & Extensions.
  2.
Under Allow in the Background, look for XQuartz (or Jeremy Huddleston Sequoia / X.Org Foundation) and make sure the toggle is ON.

I guess this is the same issue with X11 in Linux that you described in your previous email. It seems now to be an issue in MacOS too.

